;; check that does not run as CPython runs it falls into, each with its title, :kind (:design, by design; :deferred, an
;; owner's work remains), :owner (the milestone or family whose files it waits on), :why, :decided (where), :match (the
;; regexes that find the method's "RESULT REASON", test/python/libtest_judge.ae's line: "import MESSAGE", "stopped-in
;; MESSAGE", "crash MESSAGE", "not-run", or pyi's "OUTCOME REASON") and :tests (the methods named, "MODULE/TEST-ID": those
;; whose line no pattern of the class finds). A method's class is the first class of this vector that names it in
;; :tests or one of whose :match finds its line (test/reap/main.ae's, test/cover/classes.ae's and java.check's rule).
