 {:id :ast-objects
  :title "_ast's object model's rest: a non-str ** keyword unseen by a node's __init__ and __replace__, test_pickling's time"
  :kind :deferred
  :owner "PY9 (the keyword: pyi's call protocol, PY-core)"
  :why "Since 202c (queue 202) compile() of an AST object is converted and validated as CPython's (obj2ast, Python/ast.c's _PyAST_Validate), ast.parse(optimize=...) preprocessed (ast_preprocess.c), the node constructors, __replace__ and __reduce__ follow 3.14's rules (go/arbace/py/builtins_ast*.go); since queue 211 str constants are interned (intern_constants), b'' is one object and ast.parse applies the int digits limit: test_ast 213 of 217 equal on the VM. Left: a **{object(): ...} or **{FakeStr('id'): ...} keyword is refused by the call (\"keywords must be strings\", eval.go's CALL_FUNCTION_EX) before __init__ or __replace__ sees it, as pyi's calls carry keyword names as strs (kwnames []*Str) where CPython hands a builtin the dict itself (2: test_non_str_kwarg, test_replace_non_str_kwarg); test_pickling can pass its 300 s limit (every exec_tests tree pickled at protocols 0-5: it passed on the VM in queue 211's run); test_exceptions' two SyntaxError offset tests"
  :decided "survey §6.6, PYS4; the user, 2026-11-03 (PY9 beside PY6); queue 201, PY9's finding 1; queue 202, 202c (the validator, the constructors, optimize: narrowed to the rest); queue 211 (interned constants, b'', the digits limit: narrowed; the AST cycle moved to :finalization-collect)"
  :match [#"^failure <class 'code'> != <class 'ast\.Module'>" #"compile\(\) arg 1 must be a string, bytes or AST object" #"'code' object has no attribute 'body'"]
  :tests ["test_exceptions/test.test_exceptions.ExceptionTests.testSyntaxErrorNonUTF8Offset"
