 {:id :pyio-buffered
  :title "_pyio's BufferedReader: readinto past the caller's buffer, seek without the seekable check"
  :kind :design
  :owner "215 (test_zstd's entries; the fix is builtins_io's)"
  :why "pyi's io is _pyio (:pyio). _pyio's BufferedReader._readinto takes avail = min(len(_read_buf) - _read_pos, len(buf)) with no regard to what it wrote already, so a second pass over the internal buffer assigns more than the caller's buffer has left (\"memoryview assignment: lvalue and rvalue have different structures\"); and _pyio's BufferedReader.seek asks the raw stream to seek without checking raw.seekable() first, where _io's C buffered_seek raises UnsupportedOperation(\"File or stream is not seekable.\"). CPython with io = _pyio does the same (probe/ri.py of 215's report). A fix: _io.BufferedReader's readinto and seek as _io's C, before _pyio's code"
